-- title:
--   A reciprocal-sine bound for an odd outer divisor slice
-- statement:
--   Let $x\ge1$ and let $d$ be a positive odd integer with $d\le\lfloor x\rfloor$. If $\sin(2\pi\alpha d)\ne0$, the outer divisor slice of the Type I sum satisfies
--   $$|S_d|\le\frac{B(x)}{|\sin(2\pi\alpha d)|},$$
--   where $B(x)$ is the explicitly defined ordinary reciprocal budget. The assertion keeps the full support and the transferred cutoff support distinct.
-- source:
--   Terence Tao, Every odd number greater than 1 is the sum of at most five primes, https://arxiv.org/abs/1201.6656, Sections 5 and 6. Original Lean source: Theorems/Thm_TaoFivePrimes_vaughan_typeI_outer_d_reciprocal_envelope.lean, lines 25-209.

